###############################################################################
# Output (monitor) layout
#
# Sway places monitors left to right in the order it detects them, at their
# preferred mode, so nothing needs to be set here for a single monitor or when
# that order happens to be right. To pin a layout, match each monitor on its
# EDID "Make Model Serial" string (see `swaymsg -t get_outputs`) so it keeps
# its place whichever port it is plugged into, or on the connector name
# (DP-1, HDMI-A-1, eDP-1, ...). `nwg-displays` (Super+d) can write this for you.
#
# output "Vendor Model Serial" mode 1920x1080@60Hz position 0 0 scale 1
# output "Vendor Model Serial" mode 1920x1080@60Hz position 1920 0 scale 1
###############################################################################

# Wallpaper for every output
output * bg $HOME/.local/share/backgrounds/lascaille/desktop.jpg fill
